From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: edwardzhu02 <explodingtnt@foxmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:19:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] stmp3770/hp39gii: add GPMI + ECC8 NAND driver
 (read/write/erase)

Port the ExistOS stmp_gpmi.c GPMI NAND controller driver to NuttX.
Verified in EmuGII QEMU against the real 128MB hardware dump: page 0
reads back the "STMP" boot-stream magic, page 1984 matches the System
image, and a write/erase/read-back cycle on a scratch block works.

- hw/regsgpmi.h, hw/regsecc8.h, hw/regssimgpmisel.h: register headers
  copied from ExistOS (GPMI + BCH/ECC8 + pinmux)
- stmp3770_gpmi.c: DMA descriptor chains on APBH channel 4, page
  read/write/erase/copy, flash-id geometry probe (2048B page / 64B
  spare / 64 pages/block / 1024 blocks)
- ISR handlers attached via irq_attach (GPMI, GPMI_DMA, ECC8)
- GPMI_PowerUp(): clear GPMI_CTRL0 + ECC8_CTRL SFTRST/CLKGATE/AHBM_SFTRST
  (same class of bug as the LCD APBH power-up; without it the
  controllers stay held in reset and every access silently hangs)
- mtd_up.h compat shim (mtdInfo_t + portMTD* API, no FreeRTOS)
- board NAND smoke test behind CONFIG_STMP3770_NAND
---
